/-!
# Ideal-power torsion in the stalks of a complex supported on a closed subspace

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S`, let `Z ⊆ X` be a closed subspace whose
inclusion is of finite presentation, and let `Q` be an object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` all of whose
cohomology sheaves are supported on `|Z|`.  Let `x̄` be a geometric point of `X` and let
`I_x̄ ⊆ 𝒪_{X, x̄}` be the stalk of the ideal sheaf of `Z`.  Then every cohomology module of `Q`
at `x̄` is `I_x̄`-power torsion in the sense of Stacks 05E6.

The argument is the source's.  On an affine étale chart `U` the defining ideal of `Z` is the
kernel of `Γ(U) → Γ(Z ×_X U)`; it is finitely generated because `Z ×_X U → U` is a closed
immersion of finite presentation between affine schemes, and its zero locus is exactly the part
of `U` lying over `|Z|`.  Part (2) of Stacks 0859 therefore makes the sections over `U` of a
quasi-coherent module supported on `|Z|` power torsion for that ideal.  Every element of the
geometric stalk is the germ of such a section over an affine neighbourhood of `x̄`, and `I_x̄`
is generated by the germs of the defining ideal on any one affine neighbourhood, so the chart
statement passes to the stalk.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartDefiningIdeal` and `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGerm` are the
  defining ideal of a closed subspace and the germ map into the étale local ring, read on the
  ring of regular functions on an étale chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.closedSubspaceStalkIdeal` is the stalk `I_x̄` of the ideal sheaf of a
  closed subspace at a geometric point.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.definingIdealAt_fg`: the defining ideal of a closed subspace of
  finite presentation is finitely generated on every affine étale chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.preimage_chartPointsMap_range_eq_zeroLocus_definingIdealAt`: on an
  affine étale chart the points lying over the closed subspace form the zero locus of that
  ideal.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isIPowerTorsion_sections_of_supportOfSheaf_subset`: the sections of
  a supported quasi-coherent module over an affine étale chart are ideal-power torsion.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.definingIdealAt_map_eq`: between affine étale charts the defining
  ideal is carried onto the defining ideal by restriction of regular functions.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.closedSubspaceStalkIdeal_eq_map`: `I_x̄` is generated by the germs
  of the defining ideal on any one affine neighbourhood of `x̄`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isIPowerTorsion_geometricModuleStalk_of_supportOfSheaf_subset`: the
  stalk at a geometric point of a supported quasi-coherent module is `I_x̄`-power torsion.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isIPowerTorsion_geometricModuleStalk_homology_of_cohomologySupportedOn`
  is **Stacks 0AET**.

## Implementation notes

The source states the conclusion for the cohomology `Hⁿ(Q_x̄)` of the stalk of `Q` in
`D(Ab)`; what is stated here is that the stalk `Hⁿ(Q)_x̄` of the cohomology sheaf is
`I_x̄`-power torsion.  The two agree because the stalk functor at a geometric point is exact,
and that identification is not available in this development, so it is recorded in the clause
of the `@[stacks 0AET]` attribute rather than used.

The module universe is pinned to the universe `u` of the schemes: part (2) of Stacks 0859,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.sectionSupportedIn_iff_exists_pow_le_annihilator`, is available only
at `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.Modules.{u, u}`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.closedSubspaceStalkIdeal` is the span of the germs of all local
sections of the defining ideal, over all small étale neighbourhoods, so that no neighbourhood
has to be chosen; that it is the image of the defining ideal on any one *affine* neighbourhood
is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.closedSubspaceStalkIdeal_eq_map`, and in particular it is finitely
generated.  The proof of that equality needs the defining ideals at two affine charts to be
related by restriction, which is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.definingIdealAt_map_eq`: the kernel
of a surjection is carried onto the kernel in a pushout square of rings, and the square of
global sections of the two base changes of `Z` is a pushout because the square of schemes is
cartesian with affine corners.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartDefiningIdeal` and `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGerm` carry no
mathematical content: `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.definingIdealAt` is an ideal of the sections of
the `RingCat`-valued structure sheaf while `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.etaleLocalRingGerm` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRestrict` speak of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRing`, and
`Ideal.map` records the ring of the ideal in its instance arguments, so the two spellings have
to be made syntactically equal before `Ideal.map_map` and `Ideal.map_pow` apply.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AET](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AET)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0859](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0859)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05E6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05E6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03MB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03MB)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

attribute [local instance] pointTopology HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-! ### The defining ideal on an affine chart -/

/-- Over an affine étale chart, the base change of a closed subspace is affine and its map to the
chart is surjective on global sections. -/
private theorem isAffine_and_surjective_appTop_rep_snd (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) (U : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (hU : IsAffine (chartScheme U)) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffine
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (Z.2.2.rep.pullback U.1.hom)) ∧
    Function.Surjective
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom)).appTop.hom := by
  have hUaff : AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffine
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U.1.left) := hU
  have hci : AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom)) :=
    Z.2.2.property_snd U.1.hom
  exact IsClosedImmersion.isAffine_surjective_of_isAffine
    ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom))

/-- The defining ideal of a closed subspace of finite presentation is finitely generated on
every affine étale chart. -/
theorem definingIdealAt_fg (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1)
    (hZ : IsFinitePresentation B S hS Z.1.ι) (U : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (hU : IsAffine (chartScheme U)) :
    (definingIdealAt B S hS X Z (op U)).FG := by
  have hUaff : AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffine
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U.1.left) := hU
  have hfp : AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyOfFinitePresentation
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom)) :=
    hZ.1 _ _ (Z.2.2.rep.fst U.1.hom) U.1.hom (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom)
      (isEtaleChart_representablePullback B S hS
        (ObjectProperty.homMk Z.1.ι :
          (⟨Z.1.toFunctor, Z.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) ⟶ X) Z.2.2.rep U)
      U.property (Z.2.2.rep.w U.1.hom).symm
  obtain ⟨hPaff, hsurj⟩ := isAffine_and_surjective_appTop_rep_snd B S hS X Z U hU
  let _ := ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom)).appTop.hom.toAlgebra
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation
      Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U.1.left, ⊤)
      Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (Z.2.2.rep.pullback U.1.hom), ⊤) :=
    ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom)).finitePresentation_appTop
  rw [definingIdealAt_eq_ker, Scheme.Γ_map_op]
  exact Algebra.FinitePresentation.ker_fG_of_surjective (Algebra.ofId _ _) hsurj

/-- The defining ideal of a closed subspace on an étale chart, as an ideal of the ring of
regular functions on that chart. -/
noncomputable abbrev chartDefiningIdeal (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) (U : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) :
    Ideal (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 U) :=
  definingIdealAt B S hS X Z (op U)

/-- The defining ideal of a closed subspace of finite presentation is finitely generated on
every affine étale chart, read on the ring of regular functions on the chart. -/
theorem chartDefiningIdeal_fg (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1)
    (hZ : IsFinitePresentation B S hS Z.1.ι) (U : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (hU : IsAffine (chartScheme U)) :
    (chartDefiningIdeal B S hS X Z U).FG :=
  definingIdealAt_fg B S hS X Z hZ U hU

/-- On an affine étale chart the points lying over the closed subspace are the zero locus of
its defining ideal. -/
theorem preimage_chartPointsMap_range_eq_zeroLocus_definingIdealAt
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1)
    (U : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (hU : IsAffine (chartScheme U)) :
    chartPointsMap U ⁻¹' Set.range (pointsMap B S hS Z.1.toFunctor Z.1.ι) =
      (chartScheme U).zeroLocus (U := ⊤)
        (SetLike.coe (definingIdealAt B S hS X Z (op U))) := by
  have hUaff : AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffine
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U.1.left) := hU
  have hci : AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom)) :=
    Z.2.2.property_snd U.1.hom
  have hA : Set.range ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom)) =
      (chartScheme U).zeroLocus (U := ⊤)
        (SetLike.coe (definingIdealAt B S hS X Z (op U))) := by
    have h2 := Scheme.Hom.support_ker
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom))
    rw [(((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map
      (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom)).isClosedEmbedding).isClosed_range.closure_eq] at h2
    rw [← h2, ker_rep_snd_eq_ofIdealTop_definingIdealAt B S hS X Z U]
    exact Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_ofIdealTop _
  -- the cartesian square of algebraic spaces over the chart
  let Wa : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS := ⟨Z.1.toFunctor, Z.2.1⟩
  let Ua : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS :=
    ⟨yoneda.obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj U), isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS _⟩
  let Pa : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS :=
    ⟨yoneda.obj (Z.2.2.rep.pullback U.1.hom), isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS _⟩
  have hpb : IsPullback (ObjectProperty.homMk (Z.2.2.rep.fst U.1.hom) : Pa ⟶ Wa)
      (ObjectProperty.homMk (yoneda.map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom)) : Pa ⟶ Ua)
      (ObjectProperty.homMk Z.1.ι : Wa ⟶ X)
      (ObjectProperty.homMk U.1.hom : Ua ⟶ X) :=
    IsPullback.of_map_of_faithful (ObjectProperty.ι _) (Z.2.2.rep.isPullback U.1.hom)
  have hrange : Set.range (pointsMap B S hS (yoneda.obj (Z.2.2.rep.pullback U.1.hom))
        (yoneda.map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom))) =
      pointsMap B S hS (yoneda.obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj U)) U.1.hom ⁻¹'
        Set.range (pointsMap B S hS Z.1.toFunctor Z.1.ι) := by
    ext y
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨w, rfl⟩
      refine ⟨pointsMap B S hS (yoneda.obj (Z.2.2.rep.pullback U.1.hom))
        (Z.2.2.rep.fst U.1.hom) w, ?_⟩
      rw [← pointsMap_comp_apply, ← pointsMap_comp_apply]
      exact congrArg (fun t => pointsMap B S hS _ t w) (Z.2.2.rep.w U.1.hom)
    · rintro ⟨z, hz⟩
      obtain ⟨w, -, hw⟩ := exists_point_of_isPullback B S hS hpb z y hz
      exact ⟨w, hw⟩
  have hid : (pointsToScheme B S hS U.1.left) ∘
      (schemePointsHomeomorph B S hS ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj U)).symm = id := by
    funext y
    exact (schemePointsHomeomorph B S hS U.1.left).apply_symm_apply y
  rw [← hA, preimage_chartPointsMap, ← hrange, range_pointsMap_yoneda_eq_preimage,
    ← Set.preimage_comp, hid, Set.preimage_id]

/-- **The sections on an affine chart are ideal-power torsion.** For a quasi-coherent
`𝒪_X`-module whose support lies over a closed subspace `Z` of finite presentation, the sections
over an affine étale chart are power torsion for the defining ideal of `Z` on that chart. -/
theorem isIPowerTorsion_sections_of_supportOfSheaf_subset
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1)
    (hZ : IsFinitePresentation B S hS Z.1.ι)
    (G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) (hG : G.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (hsupp : supportOfSheaf B S hS X.1 (moduleAddSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2 G) ⊆
      Set.range (pointsMap B S hS Z.1.toFunctor Z.1.ι))
    (U : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (hU : IsAffine (chartScheme U)) :
    IsIPowerTorsion (chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 U) (G.val.obj (op U))
      (chartDefiningIdeal B S hS X Z U) := by
  intro s
  have hs : SectionSupportedIn B S hS X.1 X.2
      (Set.range (pointsMap B S hS Z.1.toFunctor Z.1.ι)) G U s := by
    intro y hy
    apply hsupp
    rw [supportOfSheaf_eq_iUnion_image_supportOfSection B S hS X.1 X.2]
    exact Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨U, Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨s, ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := (sectionSupportedIn_iff_exists_pow_le_annihilator B S hS X.2 G hG
    (Set.range (pointsMap B S hS Z.1.toFunctor Z.1.ι)) U hU
    (chartDefiningIdeal_fg B S hS X Z hZ U hU)
    (preimage_chartPointsMap_range_eq_zeroLocus_definingIdealAt B S hS X Z U hU) s).mp hs
  exact ⟨n + 1, n.succ_pos, fun a ha => hn a (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right n.le_succ ha)⟩

/-! ### Restriction of the defining ideal between affine charts -/

/-- In a pushout square of rings whose left map is surjective, the image of the kernel of that
map is the kernel of the opposite map. -/
private theorem map_ker_eq_of_isPushout {A C₁ C₂ D : CommRingCat.{u}} {f : A ⟶ C₁} {g : A ⟶ C₂}
    {i : C₁ ⟶ D} {j : C₂ ⟶ D} (h : IsPushout f g i j)
    (hf : Function.Surjective f.hom) :
    (RingHom.ker f.hom).map g.hom = RingHom.ker j.hom := by
  set I := (RingHom.ker f.hom).map g.hom with hI
  let q : C₂ →+* C₂ ⧸ I := Ideal.Quotient.mk I
  have hk : RingHom.ker f.hom ≤ RingHom.ker (q.comp g.hom) := fun a ha =>
    Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem g.hom ha)
  let b : C₁ →+* C₂ ⧸ I := f.hom.liftOfSurjective hf ⟨q.comp g.hom, hk⟩
  have hb : b.comp f.hom = q.comp g.hom := RingHom.liftOfSurjective_comp _ _ _
  let d : D ⟶ CommRingCat.of (C₂ ⧸ I) :=
    h.desc (CommRingCat.ofHom b) (CommRingCat.ofHom q) (CommRingCat.hom_ext hb)
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [hI, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro a ha
    change j.hom (g.hom a) = 0
    rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← h.w, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply]
    exact (congrArg i.hom ha).trans (map_zero i.hom)
  · intro a ha
    apply Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mp
    change q a = 0
    have hd := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (h.inr_desc
      (CommRingCat.ofHom b) (CommRingCat.ofHom q) (CommRingCat.hom_ext hb)) a
    change d.hom (j.hom a) = q a at hd
    rw [ha, map_zero] at hd
    exact hd.symm

/-- The base changes of a closed subspace to two étale charts are cartesian over the charts:
for a morphism `k : V ⟶ U` of étale charts of `X` the square of schemes with corners
`Z ×_X V`, `Z ×_X U`, `V` and `U` is cartesian. -/
theorem isPullback_toScheme_rep_snd (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) {U V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (k : V ⟶ U) :
    IsPullback
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (Z.2.2.rep.lift (Z.2.2.rep.fst V.1.hom)
        (Z.2.2.rep.snd V.1.hom ≫ k.hom.left)
        (representablePullback_lift_cond B S hS
          (ObjectProperty.homMk Z.1.ι :
            (⟨Z.1.toFunctor, Z.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) ⟶ X) Z.2.2.rep k)))
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (Z.2.2.rep.snd V.1.hom))
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom))
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map k.hom.left) := by
  set m := Z.2.2.rep.lift (Z.2.2.rep.fst V.1.hom) (Z.2.2.rep.snd V.1.hom ≫ k.hom.left)
    (representablePullback_lift_cond B S hS
      (ObjectProperty.homMk Z.1.ι :
        (⟨Z.1.toFunctor, Z.2.1⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) ⟶ X) Z.2.2.rep k) with hm
  have hs : IsPullback (yoneda.map m ≫ Z.2.2.rep.fst U.1.hom)
      (yoneda.map (Z.2.2.rep.snd V.1.hom)) Z.1.ι
      (yoneda.map k.hom.left ≫ U.1.hom) := by
    rw [hm, Z.2.2.rep.lift_fst, CostructuredArrow.w k.hom]
    exact Z.2.2.rep.isPullback V.1.hom
  have hp : yoneda.map m ≫ yoneda.map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom) =
      yoneda.map (Z.2.2.rep.snd V.1.hom) ≫ yoneda.map k.hom.left := by
    rw [← yoneda.map_comp, ← yoneda.map_comp, hm, Z.2.2.rep.lift_snd]
  have hpre : IsPullback (yoneda.map m) (yoneda.map (Z.2.2.rep.snd V.1.hom))
      (yoneda.map (Z.2.2.rep.snd U.1.hom)) (yoneda.map k.hom.left) :=
    IsPullback.of_right hs hp (Z.2.2.rep.isPullback U.1.hom)
  exact (IsPullback.of_map_of_faithful yoneda hpre).map (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)

/-- **The defining ideal is base changed by restriction between affine charts.** For a morphism
of affine étale charts of `X`, the ideal generated by the restrictions of the defining ideal of
a closed subspace is the defining ideal on the smaller chart. -/
theorem definingIdealAt_map_eq (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (k : V ⟶ U)
    (hU : IsAffine (chartScheme U)) (hV : IsAffine (chartScheme V)) :
    (definingIdealAt B S hS X Z (op U)).map (chartRestrict (hF := X.2) k) =
      definingIdealAt B S hS X Z (op V) := by
  have hUaff : AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffine
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U.1.left) := hU
  have hVaff : AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffine
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V.1.left) := hV
  obtain ⟨hPaff, hsurj⟩ := isAffine_and_surjective_appTop_rep_snd B S hS X Z U hU
  rw [definingIdealAt_eq_ker, definingIdealAt_eq_ker, Scheme.Γ_map_op, Scheme.Γ_map_op,
    chartRestrict_eq_appTop]
  exact map_ker_eq_of_isPushout
    (isPushout_appTop_of_isPullback (isPullback_toScheme_rep_snd B S hS X Z k)) hsurj

/-- **The defining ideal is base changed by restriction between affine charts**, read on the
rings of regular functions on the charts. -/
theorem chartDefiningIdeal_map_eq (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) {U V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (k : V ⟶ U)
    (hU : IsAffine (chartScheme U)) (hV : IsAffine (chartScheme V)) :
    (chartDefiningIdeal B S hS X Z U).map (chartRestrict (hF := X.2) k) =
      chartDefiningIdeal B S hS X Z V :=
  definingIdealAt_map_eq B S hS X Z k hU hV

/-! ### The stalk of the defining ideal at a geometric point -/

/-- The germ of a regular function on an étale chart in the étale local ring at a geometric
point, with the ring of sections over the chart as its domain. -/
noncomputable abbrev chartGerm (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (x : GeometricPoint B S hS X.1)
    (N : SmallEtaleNeighborhood x) :
    chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 N.chart →+* etaleLocalRing B S hS X.1 x :=
  etaleLocalRingGerm B S hS X.1 x (op N)

/-- The germ maps into the étale local ring are compatible with restriction of regular
functions to a smaller neighbourhood. -/
theorem chartGerm_comp_chartRestrict (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (x : GeometricPoint B S hS X.1) {N M : SmallEtaleNeighborhood x} (f : M ⟶ N) :
    (chartGerm B S hS X x M).comp (chartRestrict (hF := X.2) f.hom) =
      chartGerm B S hS X x N :=
  spaceGerm_naturality (x := x) (op f)

/-- **Stacks 0AET.** The stalk `I_x̄ ⊆ 𝒪_{X, x̄}` at a geometric point of the ideal sheaf of a
closed subspace: the ideal of the étale local ring generated by the germs of the local sections
of the defining ideal. -/
@[stacks 0AET "the stalk I_x̄ of the ideal sheaf of Z"]
noncomputable def closedSubspaceStalkIdeal (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) (x : GeometricPoint B S hS X.1) :
    Ideal (etaleLocalRing B S hS X.1 x) :=
  Ideal.span {r | ∃ (N : SmallEtaleNeighborhood x) (a : chartRing B S hS X.1 X.2 N.chart),
    a ∈ chartDefiningIdeal B S hS X Z N.chart ∧ chartGerm B S hS X x N a = r}

/-- **The stalk of the defining ideal is generated by the germs from any one affine
neighbourhood.** -/
theorem closedSubspaceStalkIdeal_eq_map (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) (x : GeometricPoint B S hS X.1)
    (N : SmallEtaleNeighborhood x) (hN : IsAffine (chartScheme N.chart)) :
    closedSubspaceStalkIdeal B S hS X Z x =
      (chartDefiningIdeal B S hS X Z N.chart).map (chartGerm B S hS X x N) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [closedSubspaceStalkIdeal, Ideal.span_le]
    rintro a ⟨M, b, hb, rfl⟩
    have hcof : IsCofiltered (SmallEtaleNeighborhood x) :=
      isCofiltered_smallEtaleNeighborhood B S hS X.1 X.2 x
    obtain ⟨W, w₁, w₂, -⟩ := IsCofilteredOrEmpty.cone_objs N M
    obtain ⟨W', l, hW'⟩ := exists_smallEtaleNeighborhoodHom_isAffine B S hS X x W
    have hb' : chartRestrict (hF := X.2) (l ≫ w₂).hom b ∈
        chartDefiningIdeal B S hS X Z W'.chart :=
      definingIdealAt_map B S hS X Z (l ≫ w₂).hom.op b hb
    rw [← chartDefiningIdeal_map_eq B S hS X Z (l ≫ w₁).hom hN hW'] at hb'
    have hmem := Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (chartGerm B S hS X x W') hb'
    rw [Ideal.map_map, chartGerm_comp_chartRestrict B S hS X x (l ≫ w₁)] at hmem
    rwa [← chartGerm_comp_chartRestrict B S hS X x (l ≫ w₂)]
  · exact Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun a ha => Ideal.subset_span ⟨N, a, ha, rfl⟩

/-! ### Power torsion in the stalk -/

/-- **The geometric stalk of a supported quasi-coherent module is ideal-power torsion.** -/
theorem isIPowerTorsion_geometricModuleStalk_of_supportOfSheaf_subset
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1)
    (hZ : IsFinitePresentation B S hS Z.1.ι)
    (G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) (hG : G.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (hsupp : supportOfSheaf B S hS X.1 (moduleAddSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2 G) ⊆
      Set.range (pointsMap B S hS Z.1.toFunctor Z.1.ι))
    (x : GeometricPoint B S hS X.1) :
    IsIPowerTorsion (etaleLocalRing B S hS X.1 x)
      (geometricModuleStalk B S hS X x G)
      (closedSubspaceStalkIdeal B S hS X Z x) := by
  intro z
  obtain ⟨N₀, s₀, hs₀⟩ := geometricModuleStalkGerm_jointly_surjective B S hS X x G z
  obtain ⟨N, l, hN⟩ := exists_smallEtaleNeighborhoodHom_isAffine B S hS X x N₀
  have hz : geometricModuleStalkGerm B S hS X x G N (G.val.map l.hom.op s₀) = z :=
    (geometricModuleStalkGerm_map B S hS X x G l s₀).trans hs₀
  obtain ⟨n, hn, hkill⟩ := isIPowerTorsion_sections_of_supportOfSheaf_subset
    B S hS X Z hZ G hG hsupp N.chart hN (G.val.map l.hom.op s₀)
  refine ⟨n, hn, fun r hr => ?_⟩
  have hle : ((chartDefiningIdeal B S hS X Z N.chart) ^ n).map (chartGerm B S hS X x N) ≤
      (Submodule.span (etaleLocalRing B S hS X.1 x) {z}).annihilator := by
    rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro a ha
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton, ← hz]
    have hs := geometricModuleStalkGerm_smul B S hS X x G N a (G.val.map l.hom.op s₀)
    rw [hkill a ha, map_zero] at hs
    exact hs.symm
  rw [closedSubspaceStalkIdeal_eq_map B S hS X Z x N hN, ← Ideal.map_pow] at hr
  exact (Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton _ _).mp (hle hr)

/-- **Stacks 0AET.** Let `X` be an algebraic space over `S`, let `Z ⊆ X` be a closed subspace
whose inclusion is of finite presentation and let `Q ∈ D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` have all its cohomology
sheaves supported on `|Z|`.  Then at every geometric point `x̄` the stalk of every cohomology
sheaf of `Q` is power torsion for the stalk `I_x̄` of the ideal sheaf of `Z`. -/
@[stacks 0AET "asserted for the stalk Hⁿ(Q)_x̄ of the cohomology sheaf rather than for the \
cohomology Hⁿ(Q_x̄) of the stalk of Q in D(Ab); the two agree by exactness of the stalk functor \
at a geometric point, which this development does not have. Stated at module universe m = u"]
theorem isIPowerTorsion_geometricModuleStalk_homology_of_cohomologySupportedOn
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    [HasSheafify (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    [(smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1) (hZ : IsFinitePresentation B S hS Z.1.ι)
    (Q : QuasicoherentDerivedCategory.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
    (hQ : CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2
      (Set.range (pointsMap B S hS Z.1.toFunctor Z.1.ι)) Q.1)
    (x : GeometricPoint B S hS X.1) (n : ℤ) :
    IsIPowerTorsion (etaleLocalRing B S hS X.1 x)
      (geometricModuleStalk B S hS X x
        ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) n).obj Q.1))
      (closedSubspaceStalkIdeal B S hS X Z x) :=
  isIPowerTorsion_geometricModuleStalk_of_supportOfSheaf_subset B S hS X Z hZ _
    (Q.property n) (hQ n) x

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

